jordan-sales: Quick heads-up — AcmeHealth wants a 2-week pilot. They specifically asked for: a Go streaming demo that shows tool/function calls + strict JSON schema output, a clear cost delta for sustained ~500 qps (with 3x short spikes), and a short security packet (SOC2 + KMS options). Can we huddle for 20m before tomorrow's sync? @nina-pre-sales @ben-eng

nina-pre-sales: Im free 9:30am PT. On pricing: for steady 500 qps Dedicated (reserved) is usually cheaper long-term. Typical numbers: hosted for bursty/low avg; reserved for sustained load. I can prepare a simple compare sheet (monthly commit scenario vs pay-as-you-go).

ben-eng: For the Go streaming sample Ill prepare a small example that shows: 1) opening a stream, 2) handling a tool_call event and invoking an external adapter, 3) feeding the adapter response back into the conversation, and 4) receiving the final structured JSON payload. Minimal pseudo-snippet: 
```
// open stream
s, _ := client.StreamCreate(ctx, req)
for ev := range s.Events() {
  if ev.Type == "tool_call" {
    // call adapter: POST /run-tool {id, inputs}
    // send adapter result back via client.SendToolResult(stream, toolResult)
  } else if ev.Type == "partial" {
    os.Stdout.Write([]byte(ev.Text))
  } else if ev.Type == "structured" {
    // ev.Payload == '{"items": [...], "confidence": 0.9}'
    // unmarshal into typed struct and persist
  }
}
```
I'll attach a runnable gist to the thread. Also recommend requesting a json_schema in the request body so the model emits machine-parseable output (helps avoid post-hoc parsing).

rachel-security: For SSO/KMS and SOC2 items: we can provide SOC2 Type II report after an NDA. KMS: hosted supports envelope encryption with customer key in our KMS; Dedicated supports customer-managed keys (AWS/GCP). Private can accept HSM or on-prem key material. Audit log retention: default 90d hosted, configurable on Dedicated/Private. If they need Bring-Your-Own-Key (BYOK) for persisted model caches, flag. I can draft answers to the typical security questionnaire fields (encryption, access controls, incident response).

diego-ps: Pre-call checklist I use for pilots: 1) sample request/response sizes (avg tokens in/out), 2) examples of tool calls we need to wire up, 3) concurrency vs QPS mapping (how they count qps), 4) SSO type (SAML/OIDC), 5) KMS expectations (BYOK/HSM?), 6) goals for latency & cost. Also ask them to share a 24hr traffic trace if possible.

quote-bot: Quote Q-5543 generated (reserved estimate) 00k monthly commit placeholder included 1 link: https://console.redwood/quotes/Q-5543

jordan-sales: Great — locking 9:30am PT. @ben-eng please include a tiny sample json_schema (e.g., expected fields + types) in your gist. @rachel-security please add a one-page KMS/SOC2 summary to share. I'll ask AcmeHealth for a trace and a couple of example payloads before the meeting. :rocket:
